format 1
adapter feed 1
npc: npc-ada

post ft-ada-chest-daily
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"daily"}

text:
    ooh a daily chest, opened. a tiny sparkle for a tiny habit. yay you~

post ft-ada-chest-weekly
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"weekly"}

text:
    the weekly chest is open. every quest of the week, done. that's SO many little steps hehe~

post ft-ada-first-lesson
kind: celebrate
trigger: first_lesson
chip: lesson

text:
    your first lesson is done: “{lesson}”. hehe, i knew you could. every big thing starts tiny~

post ft-ada-lesson-alpha-beta-gamma-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"alpha-beta-gamma"}

text:
    “{lesson}” is done. alpha is a chunk, beta is a fast electron, and gamma isn't a particle at all. three little surprises, hehe

post ft-ada-lesson-alpha-beta-gamma-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"alpha-beta-gamma","perfect":true}

text:
    a perfect score in “{lesson}”. three kinds of radiation and this learner can tell them ALL apart. eee, so clever~

post ft-ada-lesson-decay-chains-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"decay-chains"}

text:
    “{lesson}” is done. one decay isn't always the end. every step makes a different nucleus, like a tiny staircase

post ft-ada-lesson-decay-chains-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"decay-chains"}

text:
    someone just followed a nucleus as it changed again and again until it was stable. nothing vanishes, it just keeps becoming

post ft-ada-lesson-half-life-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"half-life"}

text:
    you finished “{lesson}”. half-life belongs to a whole crowd of atoms. it's not a little timer inside each one. hehe

post ft-ada-lesson-half-life-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"half-life","perfect":true}

text:
    a perfect “{lesson}”. start with 100 nuclei and after one half-life about 50 are left. note the word about. i love that word~

post ft-ada-lesson-radioactivity-is-natural-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"radioactivity-is-natural"}

text:
    you finished “{lesson}”. it's in rocks, in the air, in food, in you, and it was here long before people. so old, so cute~

post ft-ada-lesson-radioactivity-is-natural-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"radioactivity-is-natural"}

text:
    someone just learned a banana is a little bit radioactive. radioactive doesn't automatically mean dangerous. banana fact of the day

post ft-ada-lesson-why-nuclei-decay-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"why-nuclei-decay"}

text:
    you finished “{lesson}”. an unstable nucleus can change all by itself, and nobody can say when. ooh, a little mystery~

post ft-ada-lesson-why-nuclei-decay-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"why-nuclei-decay"}

text:
    someone just learned the parent and the daughter. one nucleus turns into another. nothing just vanishes, it only becomes something new. so cute

post ft-ada-quests
kind: celebrate
trigger: daily_quests_done
chip: quests

text:
    all the daily quests are claimed. go open the chest, i think it's sparkly~

post ft-ada-rank-passed
kind: celebrate
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed"}

text:
    you passed {rival} in the weekly ranking. eep, so quick. keep going, friend~

post ft-ada-checkpoint-radioactivity
kind: milestone
trigger: checkpoint_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity"}
reactors: npc-hal

text:
    the {unit} checkpoint is passed. take a little moment. you earned every bit of it~

post ft-ada-testout-radioactivity
kind: milestone
trigger: testout_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity"}
reactors: npc-hal

text:
    you tested out of “{unit}”. you already knew all this and now it's on your record. so sparkly~

post ft-ada-unit-inside-the-atom-1
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"inside-the-atom"}
reactors: npc-hal

text:
    someone just finished “{unit}” with Hal. they know what's inside an atom. now they can find out how a nucleus changes, and that part is mine. hehe~

post ft-ada-unit-radioactivity-2
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity"}
reactors: npc-hal

text:
    you finished “{unit}”. now you know why nuclei change, what comes out, and how a crowd follows a pattern. radioactivity is a natural part of the world

post ft-ada-comeback-14
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":14}

text:
    welcome back, {name}. the door was open the whole time and i kept the flask warm. let's find where you stopped

post ft-ada-comeback-3
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":3}

text:
    there you are, {name}. i saved your seat~ ready for one more tiny lesson?

post ft-ada-rank-passed-by
kind: nudge
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed_by"}

text:
    oh no, {rival} passed you in the weekly ranking. just one more lesson and you could zoom ahead again

post ft-ada-tease-radioactivity
kind: tease
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity","lessonId":"half-life"}

text:
    half-life is done, yay~ next you'll follow a nucleus that changes again and again. one decay isn't always the end
